# Requirements this host cannot enforce

Generated by the NIST 800-171r3 Rocky 9 overlay, version {{ meta.version }},
from `catalog/overlay-rocky9.yml`. Managed by Ansible; edits are overwritten.

800-171r3 has {{ requirements | length }} active security requirements, and
this overlay classifies each by what a Rocky Linux 9 host can actually
enforce: {{ technical | length }} technical, {{ partial | length }} partial, {{ organizational | length }} organizational.
The {{ organizational | length }} in the first table below are **not** satisfied by any host
configuration; the {{ partial | length }} in the second are only partly satisfied. Each needs a
documented organizational control before this system may be authorized to
process CUI.

The assessment tool reports the organizational ones as `NOT_APPLICABLE(host)`
and the partial ones as `MANUAL`, never as `PASS`, so a clean assessment never
implies the organization's obligations are met.

