## Organization-defined parameters ({{ org_odp | length }})

800-171r3 leaves these values to the organization, and no host setting can
satisfy them: they are review frequencies, notification periods, named
authorities, and policy statements. The values below are the ones this
deployment has committed to. Cite them in the SSP; they are the answer to
"[Assignment: organization-defined ...]" for each requirement listed.

A technical requirement can still appear here. The host enforcing least
privilege, for example, does not review who holds it — that review is
{{ (org_odp | selectattr('id', 'equalto', 'priv_review') | first).value
   | default('an organizational obligation', true) }}, and a human owes it.

Parameters the host *does* enforce are not in this table. They are asserted by
the assessor on every run, so the report is their evidence.

